<title>SWEDEN: Autoliv posts 14 pct gain in 9 mo profit.</title>
<headline>Autoliv posts 14 pct gain in 9 mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish car safety equipment maker Autoliv reports for the nine months to September 30.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		   863  vs    758</p>
<p> Sales					8,552  vs  7,765</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)			     10.22  vs   8.70</p>
<p> Operating costs			   7,331 vs  6,753</p>
<p> Operating profit pre deprec	   1,221 vs  1,012</p>
<p> Depreciation				  401 vs    319</p>
<p> Operating profit after deprec	   820 vs    693</p>
<p> Associate interest			   38 vs     22</p>
<p> Net financial items		  CREDIT 5 vs     43 CREDIT</p>
<p> Tax					     298 vs    280</p>
<p> Minorities					3 vs	0</p>
<p> Net profit				    562 vs    478</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found the average of eight analysts was for a profit after financial items and before tax of 870 million crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
